+# VortexRealm – handoff for the next AI agent
+
+Read this first. It is everything you need to take over: the server, the repo, how to build and release, where
+things live in the code, what happened so far and what is still open.
+
+## 1. Who / what
+
+- **Server:** the user's Minecraft server on **Bao Host** — `vortexsmps.playwithbao.com`, **Paper 1.21.11**,
+  offline mode with **AuthMe**, **low memory** (out-of-memory crashes have happened; keep everything light).
+- **VortexRealm** is the main jar: **Practice (MCPVP-style ranked duels, tiers, FFA, bots, lobby) + SMP (homes, tpa,
+  rtp, warps, trade, market…) in one plugin.** This is what runs on the server.
+- **PracticePvP** is the same code under the old name (`net.practicepvp`, `practice.*` perms, `pp_*` tables). It is the
+  **source of truth**; VortexRealm is generated from it.
+- **VortexSMP is retired** (merged into VortexRealm in 3.8.0). Its update entry tells servers to remove it.
+
+## 2. Repo
+
+- GitHub: **`Rayanboonty/3Dmodel`** (public), folder **`vortex-realm/`**.
+- Branch: **`claude/vortex-realm-pvp-plugin-2x1tq1`** — the only branch to use. **Never push to `main`. No PRs.**
+- The repo root also holds unrelated 3D files (`.glb`, `.blend`, `.mp4`, `index.html`) — leave them alone.
+
+```
+vortex-realm/
+  practicepvp/      SOURCE OF TRUTH (net.practicepvp). Edit here.
+  vortexrealm/      GENERATED by tools/make_vortex.py. Never edit by hand.
+  vortexsmp/        retired SMP plugin (kept for reference)
+  vortexpvp/        test build (generated by tools/make_vortexpvp.py from practicepvp + vortexpvp-plus/)
+  vortexpvp-plus/   add-on systems for the VortexPvP test build
+  dist/             released jars, SHA256SUMS, update.json (the auto-update manifest), screenshots
+  tools/
+    make_vortex.py          practicepvp/ -> vortexrealm/   (2.x.y -> 3.x.y)
+    vortexrealm-extra/      files laid on top of vortexrealm/ (VortexMigration.java)
+    make_update_json.py     writes dist/update.json
+    make_vortexpvp.py       practicepvp/ -> vortexpvp/ (test build)
+  pom.xml           parent pom (modules practicepvp, vortexrealm, vortexsmp)
+  README.md         user-facing changelog, one section per release
+  HANDOFF.md        this file
+```
+
+### Push access (important)
+
+The second agent's session (Nov 17 2026) was signed in to GitHub as **`mroudani-cyber`**, which has **no push access**
+to `Rayanboonty/3Dmodel` — it could only clone. To push, the user must either:
+1. add `mroudani-cyber` as a collaborator on `Rayanboonty/3Dmodel` (GitHub → repo Settings → Collaborators) **and**
+   install the Claude GitHub App on that repo (https://github.com/apps/claude/installations/select_target), or
+2. connect the `Rayanboonty` GitHub account to Claude (https://claude.ai/connect-github) and start a new session with
+   the repo selected.
+
+Then attach it with `add_repo` (owner `Rayanboonty`, repo `3Dmodel`, access `push`).
+
+### Network (important)
+
+Building needs **`repo.papermc.io`** (Paper API) and **`repo.extendedclip.com`** (PlaceholderAPI). The default cloud
+environment blocks both, so Maven fails with "Could not transfer artifact … paper-api". The user has to allow these
+two hosts (a cloud environment with them in its allowed hosts), otherwise no jar can be built.
+
+## 3. Build
+
+From `vortex-realm/`:
+
+```bash
+mvn -q -o package -DskipTests -pl practicepvp     # drop -o on a fresh machine (empty ~/.m2)
+python3 -I tools/make_vortex.py                     # regenerate vortexrealm/ from practicepvp/
+mvn -q -o package -DskipTests -pl vortexrealm
+# -> practicepvp/target/PracticePvP-2.x.y.jar, vortexrealm/target/VortexRealm-3.x.y.jar
+```
+
+**Version bump:** change only `practicepvp/pom.xml` line 9 (`<version>2.x.y</version>`). `make_vortex.py` reads it and
+writes `3.x.y` into `vortexrealm/pom.xml` by itself (major + 1).
+
+**About make_vortex.py:** the original script lived only in the first agent's scratchpad and was lost. It was rebuilt on
+Nov 17 2026 from the committed output and **reproduces `vortexrealm/` 3.9.2 byte for byte from `practicepvp/` 2.9.2**
+(checked with `git status` after a run: no differences). What it does: renames the package and main class, `pp_*` →
+`vr_*` tables, `practice.*` → `vortex.*` permissions, `PracticePvP` → `VortexRealm` in Java, `database.name` default
+`vortexrealm`, PlaceholderAPI id `vortex`, backup folder `VortexRealm-2-Vault` (in `DataVault` only), adds the
+"PracticePvP is installed too" guard, `VortexMigration.autoMigrate()` and the `/vortex` command, and fixes plugin.yml /
+messages.yml / default-kits.yml / admin.html texts. Every patch uses an exact match and stops with "patch failed" if
+the source changed under it — then update the patch in the script.
+
+After running it, `git diff --stat vortexrealm` should only show the changes you made in `practicepvp/`.
+
+## 4. Release / auto-update
+
+1. Build both jars (above). Copy them into `dist/` as `PracticePvP-2.x.y.jar` and `VortexRealm-3.x.y.jar`.
+2. Edit `NOTES` in `tools/make_update_json.py` (one short line per plugin; keep the VortexSMP "remove this plugin" note).
+3. `python3 -I tools/make_update_json.py` → rewrites `dist/update.json` with the newest jar of each plugin + SHA-256.
+4. Append the two jars to `dist/SHA256SUMS`: `cd dist && sha256sum PracticePvP-2.x.y.jar VortexRealm-3.x.y.jar >> SHA256SUMS`.
+5. Add a `## 3.x.y / 2.x.y — title` section at the end of `README.md`.
+6. Commit with the message style `VortexRealm 3.x.y / PracticePvP 2.x.y: what changed`, ending with the attribution
+   trailer lines your session gives you (`Co-Authored-By: …` and `Claude-Session: …`).
+7. `git push -u origin claude/vortex-realm-pvp-plugin-2x1tq1` — retry up to 4 times with backoff on network errors.
+8. Send the user the new `dist/VortexRealm-3.x.y.jar`.
+
+Servers read `update.json` from
+`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Rayanboonty/3Dmodel/refs/heads/claude/vortex-realm-pvp-plugin-2x1tq1/vortex-realm/dist/update.json`
+(`update/AutoUpdater.java`): it downloads the jar, checks the SHA-256, puts it in the update folder and restarts when
+nobody is online. **`/pvpadmin update`** checks and installs right away. So a push to the branch = an update on the server.
+
+## 5. Architecture map (paths under `practicepvp/src/main/java/net/practicepvp/`)
+
+| Where | What |
+|---|---|
+| `PracticePlugin.java` | main class (→ `VortexRealm.java`); starts every part through `module(...)`, so one broken part doesn't kill the rest |
+| `smp/ModeManager.java` | worlds and their modes (`worlds.yml`), **inventory groups** per world group, inventory **backups**, **pending restore** for offline players (applied on join) |
+| `smp/SmpRestore.java` | brings SMP data back from a Data Vault snapshot, old plugin files/zips, old VortexSMP folders (homes, warps, inventories, ender chests, XP) |
+| `smp/PlayerDat.java` | reads `world/playerdata/<uuid>.dat` offline (inventory, armour, ender chest, XP, world, group marker) |
+| `smp/` (Hub, ServerSelector, WorldMode, ModeRules, ServerLink) | hub, world selector, per-world rules |
+| `survival/*` | the ported SMP (was VortexSMP): `survival/VortexSMP.java`, homes/tpa/rtp/warps/back, combat tag, trade, market, drills; files in `plugins/<plugin>/smp/`; own `survival/config/Opt.java`/`Cfg.java` |
+| `arena/ArenaSeal.java` | invisible barrier walls around arenas — since 3.9.2 low (20 blocks above), one arena at a time, vanilla maps skipped (memory fix) |
+| `arena/*` | arenas, generator, per-match instances, resets (`ChangeTracker`, `RegionSnapshot`, `BlockJobs`) |
+| `data/DataVault.java` | full backups outside the plugin folder (`plugins/VortexRealm-2-Vault` for VortexRealm, `VortexRealm-Vault` for PracticePvP); auto-restore if the plugin folder is lost. Automatic backups are **off** since 3.9.1 (Backup Everything button) |
+| `data/OldDataImport.java` | an old plugin folder / zip dropped in `plugins/<plugin>/import/` is brought back on the next start |
+| `data/Database.java`, `Upgrader.java` | SQLite/MySQL tables, upgrade steps + update report |
+| `build/ClubSpawnDesign.java` + `resources/lobbies/club_spawn.vrmap` | "Club Spawn" lobby (Bedrock map converted to Java; palette + run-length columns) |
+| `dialog/SmpDialogs.java` | `/pvpadmin` → SMP page (on/off, settings, worlds, bring back data, player inventories) |
+| `dialog/AdminDialogs.java`, `gui/admin/*` | the rest of `/pvpadmin` |
+| `config/Opt.java` + `config/Cfg.java` | every setting: `Opt` = definition (path, type, default, section, name, help), `Cfg` = reading them |
+| `update/AutoUpdater.java` | auto-update from `update.json` |
+| `command/AdminCommands.java` | `/pvpadmin <sub>` |
+| `bot/`, `ffa/`, `duel/`, `queue/`, `match/`, `kit/`, `rank/`, `social/`, `staff/`, `lobby/`, `npc/`, `deco/`, `web/`, `ai/` | practice bots, FFA, duels, queues, matches, kits, tiers, friends/tab, staff tools, lobby, NPCs, decorations, web panel, `/ai` assistant |
+| `tools/vortexrealm-extra/main/java/net/vortexrealm/VortexMigration.java` | VortexRealm only: moves a PracticePvP install over (files, `pp_*`→`vr_*`, perms), `/vortex migrate` |
+
+## 6. Admin commands cheat sheet
+
+- `/pvpadmin` (`/pa`) — admin panel (settings, kits, arenas, SMP page, Data Vault, ranks…)
+- `/pvpadmin update` — check `update.json` and install now
+- `/pvpadmin selftest` · `health` · `reload`
+- `/pvpadmin backupall` / `fullbackup` / `fullrestore` / `vault` / `backups` / `restore` — Data Vault
+- `/pvpadmin invbackup` / `invbackups` / `setinv` — inventory backups
+- `/pvpadmin kitbackup` / `kitrestore` · `settingsbackup` / `settingsrestore`
+- `/pvpadmin smp` — SMP page · `/pvpadmin arenas enableall` · `arena …` · `walls` · `rebuild` · `vanilla`
+- `/pvpadmin setlobby` · `forcelobby` · `hub` · `winter` · `bothall [remove]` · `tabdesign <name>` · `maintenance`
+- `/pvpadmin elo|tier|skill|ranked|unranked <player> …` · `player <name>` · `staff`
+- `/vortex [migrate]` (VortexRealm only) · `/ai` · `/ecospawn` · `/smpadmin`, `/setspawn`, `/setwarp`, `/delwarp`
+- Permissions: `vortex.*` in VortexRealm (`practice.*` in PracticePvP), SMP uses `vortexsmp.*`.
+
